ENTRY            M0293   20261015   20261127   20261127       M149
SUBENT        M0293001   20261015   20261127   20261127       M149
BIB                 14         48
TITLE      Nucleon branches and a half-line mechanism for decay
            of the giant resonance of a Na-23 nucleus.
AUTHOR     (A.S.Gabelko,K.M.Irgashev,B.S.Ishkhanov,I.M.Kapitonov,
            I.M.Piskarev)
INSTITUTE  (4RUSMOS)
REFERENCE  (J,MUPB,42,(1),26,1987)
            English translation of VMU,42,(1),24,1987.
           (J,VMU,42,(1),24,1987)
FACILITY   (BETAT,4RUSMOS) 32 MeV betatron.
INC-SOURCE (BRST) Obtained in internal 0.1 mm platinum target.
METHOD     (EXTB,SITA) Measurement of gamma-ray spectra obtained
            at disintegration of giant dipole resonance  of  the
            final  nuclei  31P  and  32S  was  made in identical
            conditions.
DETECTOR   (GELI) With  volume of 100 cm**3 placed at a distance
            of 35 cm from the beam axis.  Energy  resolution  is
            3.5 keV for gamma-rays with energy 1.332 MeV.
PART-DET   (G) Gamma detection at 140 deg.
ANALYSIS   To obtain  the  absolute  value  of  integral   cross
            sections   the   relative   method   was  used:  the
            experimental gamma-spectra were compared  with  well
            known spectrum (gamma,x gamma') reactions.
REL-REF    (N,,U.R.Arzibekov+,J,YF,40,1121,1984)
           (N,,U.R.Arzibekov+,J,YF,42,1059,1985)
            Experiment method presented in detail.
ERR-ANALYS No information.
COMMENT    The aim  of this work was to estimate the probability
            of semidirect disintegration in partial photonuclear
            channels  for  23Na  nucleus. The  integrated  cross
            section for 23Na(gamma,p(I)) and 23Na(gamma,n(I))
            reactions and the semidirect components were obtained.
           Determination  of  the  nature  of  gamma line, i.e.
            identification of transitions between levels of the
            final nuclei leading to appearance of maxima in the
            spectrum,   was   achieved   taking   into  account
            information for cascade gamma transitions.
HISTORY    (19900319C)
           (19910202A) Corrected by V.Varlamov, V.Mclane.
           (19981111A) Corrected by V.Varlamov.
           (19990429A) Date is corrected.
           (20180213A) Corrected by SD and VV: REFERENCE,
            STATUS, REACTION, DATA, lowercase.
           (20220114A) Corrected by V.Varlamov: PART-DET, EN-SEC
            in SUBENT 003 deleted, COMMENT in SUBENTs 002, 003.
           (20220429A) Corrected by V.Varlamov: REACTION.
           (20261015A) Corrected by V.Varlamov: TITLE, AUTHOR,
            REFERENCE, PART-DET, ERR-ANALYS, COMMENT, COMMON,
            REACTION, STATUS.
